{{/*
The smoke family's defect: the named method panics.

A panicking method is what the smoke check exists for, and the reason it
is the weakest check that catches the most — a subject that dies on an
ordinary value fails every other check too, but only this one reports the
method that did it instead of a crashed run.

The override's parameters are blanked because the body reads none of
them, and its results are unnamed because it never reaches a return.
*/}}
{{- define "suite.defect.stub-panic" -}}
{{ renderExpr (external $.Prove "One") }}({{ printf "%q" .DefectName }},
	func(tb {{ renderExpr (external "testing" "TB") }}) {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Subject) }} {
		return {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Ctor) }}(tb, {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Option) }}(
			func{{ renderParams .AnonParams }} {{ renderReturns .AnonReturns }} {
				panic({{ printf "%q" .PanicMessage }})
			}))
	}){{ template "suite.frag.defect-reason" . }}
{{- end -}}
